1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,320
My wife and I built Lullwatch because of our

2
00:00:02,320 --> 00:00:03,880
own first pregnancy.

3
00:00:03,880 --> 00:00:05,560
When the contraction started,

4
00:00:05,580 --> 00:00:08,900
we had one question and nothing we had could answer it.

5
00:00:08,900 --> 00:00:09,880
Is this it?

6
00:00:09,880 --> 00:00:12,200
Do we go now or do we wait?

7
00:00:12,200 --> 00:00:13,660
We learned that this is one of the hardest

8
00:00:13,660 --> 00:00:15,420
calls in late pregnancy.

9
00:00:15,520 --> 00:00:18,020
Go in too early and you're sent home.

10
00:00:18,160 --> 00:00:21,240
In a study of over 1,600 first-time mothers,

11
00:00:21,240 --> 00:00:23,260
one in three went to hospital before their

12
00:00:23,260 --> 00:00:25,540
contractions were five minutes apart.

13
00:00:25,540 --> 00:00:27,860
Those early arrivals were more likely to end

14
00:00:27,860 --> 00:00:30,520
in a caesarean, about one in four,

15
00:00:30,520 --> 00:00:32,300
against about one in six,

16
00:00:32,320 --> 00:00:34,660
but leave it too late and the journey itself

17
00:00:34,660 --> 00:00:36,080
becomes the risk.

18
00:00:36,080 --> 00:00:37,820
So we looked for an app to help,

19
00:00:37,820 --> 00:00:39,780
but the apps that could help want the most

20
00:00:39,780 --> 00:00:41,640
private data there is.

21
00:00:41,640 --> 00:00:45,140
When Mozilla reviewed 25 pregnancy and period apps,

22
00:00:45,140 --> 00:00:47,340
18 got its privacy warning.

23
00:00:47,340 --> 00:00:48,760
And in 2025,

24
00:00:48,900 --> 00:00:51,160
a US jury found Meta liable for collecting

25
00:00:51,160 --> 00:00:54,680
data from the Flo app, including pregnancy data.

26
00:00:54,980 --> 00:00:57,260
So we built Lullwatch, a private labour

27
00:00:57,260 --> 00:00:59,380
companion that tells her when to pack and when

28
00:00:59,380 --> 00:01:00,820
to leave for the hospital.

29
00:01:00,860 --> 00:01:04,040
Its AI runs on sealed hardware on NEAR AI Cloud,

30
00:01:04,040 --> 00:01:06,020
and her own phone checks the proof.

31
00:01:06,080 --> 00:01:07,840
Setup is three questions.

32
00:01:07,920 --> 00:01:10,180
Is this her first baby, which hospital,

33
00:01:10,180 --> 00:01:12,060
and how long the journey takes?

34
00:01:12,280 --> 00:01:14,700
Lullwatch applies the standard rule for her,

35
00:01:14,700 --> 00:01:16,760
if her midwife gave her different numbers,

36
00:01:16,760 --> 00:01:17,740
those win.

37
00:01:17,900 --> 00:01:20,380
When a contraction starts, she taps.

38
00:01:20,480 --> 00:01:22,700
When it ends, she taps again.

39
00:01:22,800 --> 00:01:26,620
Or, hands-free, she just says now, and stop.

40
00:01:26,620 --> 00:01:28,660
The log never leaves her phone.

41
00:01:29,080 --> 00:01:31,680
A few hours in, the gaps are shrinking.

42
00:01:31,760 --> 00:01:34,420
Fixed, tested rules watch the trend,

43
00:01:34,420 --> 00:01:36,980
forecast when she'll meet her midwife's rule,

44
00:01:36,980 --> 00:01:39,800
subtract the journey, and give her a time,

45
00:01:39,800 --> 00:01:41,020
start packing,

46
00:01:41,020 --> 00:01:42,620
leave by this time.

47
00:01:42,720 --> 00:01:44,460
When it's time to call the maternity unit,

48
00:01:44,460 --> 00:01:46,480
she doesn't have to think.

49
00:01:46,540 --> 00:01:48,260
She taps Call midwife,

50
00:01:48,260 --> 00:01:50,660
and the sealed AI writes exactly what to say

51
00:01:50,660 --> 00:01:52,220
from her timer.

52
00:01:52,220 --> 00:01:53,880
Every number is checked against the timer

53
00:01:53,880 --> 00:01:55,400
before she sees it.

54
00:01:55,400 --> 00:01:56,640
And if something feels wrong,

55
00:01:56,640 --> 00:01:58,020
like bleeding,

56
00:01:58,040 --> 00:01:59,800
or the baby moving less,

57
00:01:59,820 --> 00:02:01,620
the count doesn't matter anymore.

58
00:02:01,720 --> 00:02:03,580
Lullwatch says go now.

59
00:02:03,740 --> 00:02:04,460
Rules decide.

60
00:02:04,460 --> 00:02:06,920
The AI only explains.

61
00:02:07,320 --> 00:02:08,900
She can ask it anything.

62
00:02:08,940 --> 00:02:11,320
Her question is encrypted on her phone to a

63
00:02:11,320 --> 00:02:13,800
key only the sealed hardware holds.

64
00:02:13,880 --> 00:02:15,840
Then her phone checks for itself,

65
00:02:15,840 --> 00:02:17,800
NVIDIA confirms the GPUs,

66
00:02:18,440 --> 00:02:20,900
Intel confirms the enclave is up to date,

67
00:02:20,900 --> 00:02:23,420
and every reply is signed inside it.

68
00:02:23,660 --> 00:02:25,500
Nobody can read her labour,

69
00:02:25,500 --> 00:02:26,680
not even us.

70
00:02:26,840 --> 00:02:29,000
That's what NEAR AI Cloud makes possible.

71
00:02:29,280 --> 00:02:31,080
Private AI you can verify,

72
00:02:31,160 --> 00:02:32,460
not just trust.

73
00:02:32,940 --> 00:02:35,060
We built the app we wished we'd had.

74
00:02:35,080 --> 00:02:37,300
Lullwatch is free, open source,

75
00:02:37,300 --> 00:02:38,500
and works offline.

76
00:02:38,920 --> 00:02:40,260
Know when to go.
